                <pb facs="0618" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg512"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé Sleeper.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-07-20"><hi rendition="#italic">July 20,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bacon instructs the legation to make immediate inquiry into and send a full
                    report of an outrage which, as represented to President, has been committed in
                    the arrest of Miss Millie Brown, Lou Giltner, and young Augustine, Isle of
                    Pines.)</p>
            </div>
